{# AC-033: semantic HTML at every width. Wide layouts follow the original 720-unit compositions; the phone layouts stay unchanged. #}

{% macro moneyVersusProof() %}
<figure class="article-figure article-figure-responsive">
<div class="article-figure-desktop figure-wide figure-wide-plot" role="group" aria-label="The five options plotted on money against proof">
<div class="figure-wide-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="figure-wide-zone" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<p class="figure-wide-warning">Real money on a guess</p>
<p class="figure-wide-y">Money</p>
<span class="figure-wide-tick figure-wide-y-low">0</span>
<span class="figure-wide-tick figure-wide-y-high">5</span>
<span class="figure-wide-tick figure-wide-x-low">0</span>
<span class="figure-wide-tick figure-wide-x-high">5</span>
<p class="figure-wide-x">Proof — how much of the number is fact, not hope</p>
<ul class="figure-wide-points" role="list">
<li class="figure-wide-point" style="--x:544;--y:114"><span class="figure-wide-label">Fix the process</span><span class="sr-only">: Money 4, Proof 4</span></li>
<li class="figure-wide-point figure-wide-point-left" style="--x:432;--y:114"><span class="figure-wide-label">Buy a CRM add-on</span><span class="sr-only">: Money 4, Proof 3</span></li>
<li class="figure-wide-point" style="--x:432;--y:60"><span class="figure-wide-label">Automate with AI</span><span class="sr-only">: Money 5, Proof 3</span></li>
<li class="figure-wide-point figure-wide-point-left is-watch" style="--x:320;--y:60"><span class="figure-wide-label">Build custom</span><span class="sr-only">: Money 5, Proof 2; in the shaded corner</span></li>
<li class="figure-wide-point figure-wide-point-left figure-wide-point-low" style="--x:656;--y:330"><span class="figure-wide-label">Do nothing</span><span class="sr-only">: Money 0, Proof 5</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="article-figure-mobile">
<div class="figure-plot">
<p class="figure-plot-axis figure-plot-y">Money, 0 to 5</p>
<div class="figure-plot-area">
<div class="figure-plot-zone"></div>
<p class="figure-plot-zone-label">Real money on a guess</p>
<ol class="figure-plot-points">
<li style="--proof:4;--money:4"><span>1</span></li>
<li style="--proof:3;--money:4"><span>2</span></li>
<li style="--proof:3;--money:5"><span>3</span></li>
<li class="is-watch" style="--proof:2;--money:5"><span>4</span></li>
<li style="--proof:5;--money:0"><span>5</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
<p class="figure-plot-axis figure-plot-x">Proof, 0 to 5 — how much of the number is fact, not hope</p>
</div>
<ol class="figure-key">
<li><span class="figure-key-mark">1</span><span>Fix the process <span class="figure-key-score">Money 4 · Proof 4</span></span></li>
<li><span class="figure-key-mark">2</span><span>Buy a CRM add-on <span class="figure-key-score">Money 4 · Proof 3</span></span></li>
<li><span class="figure-key-mark">3</span><span>Automate with AI <span class="figure-key-score">Money 5 · Proof 3</span></span></li>
<li class="is-watch"><span class="figure-key-mark">4</span><span>Build custom <span class="figure-key-score">Money 5 · Proof 2</span></span></li>
<li><span class="figure-key-mark">5</span><span>Do nothing <span class="figure-key-score">Money 0 · Proof 5</span></span></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figcaption>The worked example from step 5, plotted. The shaded corner is the pair to watch: a big number nobody has checked.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro decisionPath() %}
<figure class="article-figure article-figure-responsive">
<div class="article-figure-desktop figure-wide figure-wide-path" role="group" aria-label="The eight steps, and the point where you stop">
<ol class="figure-wide-steps" role="list">
<li><span>Ask where the business loses money</span></li>
<li><span>Pull the real numbers</span></li>
<li><span>Sort them: facts, fair guesses, unknowns</span></li>
<li><span>Write down all five options</span></li>
<li><span>Score every option, money against proof</span></li>
<li><span>Choose, and write down why</span>
<p class="figure-wide-exit"><strong>Nothing clears the bar?</strong><span>Stop. Say so out loud.</span></p></li>
<li><span>Run one 90-day test with a stop rule</span></li>
<li><span>Ask six questions before you approve spend</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="article-figure-mobile">
<ol class="figure-flow">
<li><span>Ask where the business loses money</span></li>
<li><span>Pull the real numbers</span></li>
<li><span>Sort them: facts, fair guesses, unknowns</span></li>
<li><span>Write down all five options</span></li>
<li><span>Score every option, money against proof</span></li>
<li><span>Choose, and write down why</span>
<p class="figure-flow-exit"><strong>Nothing clears the bar?</strong> Stop. Say so out loud.</p></li>
<li><span>Run one 90-day test with a stop rule</span></li>
<li><span>Ask six questions before you approve spend</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figcaption>Two hours of work, and a real exit. Most of the method happens before anyone writes a line of code.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endmacro %}
